From f0d188e0103971ce1cb024944baefb9cb3931569 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Olivier Louvignes <olivier@mgcrea.io>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 06:35:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/57] clk: ingenic: add the X1600 CGU driver

The register layout comes from the clock tables of the vendor kernel
running on a HiBy R1 (read from its memory), and every rate was checked
against its clk_summary. The X1600's CDR registers match the X1830's,
but its PLLs do not: rate = ext * M / (N * OD1 * OD0), with no offsets
or encodings, so they get custom read-only clock ops. The CPU, L2, AHB,
APB and DDR clocks are read-only as well. I2S, CAN, CDBUS and the
memory power gates are left out for now.
